# The coordinator waits a thousand times its Down bound before it re-places
# a down machine's roles: in practice it never re-places them. Since #909
# (oracles that do not judge) the heal oracle judges every seed from the
# audit's configuration in force, and excuses only a journal with a gone
# member on a seed whose Down bound reaches past its window. It survived
# while every machine the sim took down came back in the tail and rejoined
# its journals in place (600 seeds green on PR #925). Since #909 the
# gone-machine scenario holds its machine down until the heal check judged,
# when it does not come back soon: only a re-placement heals its journals.
# The excuse is the drawn Down bound against the heal window, which no
# mutant of the coordinator widens, so the proof is red where it does not
# fire. The scenario strikes about once in 300 seeds, so the fixed 600
# seeds may hold no strike (survived on PR #962 with a coin on the hold).
excuse: skip heal: re-place past tail
expect: either #773
file: crates/lib/paros-coordinator/src/cell/watch.rs
--- find
        if now.saturating_sub(since) < self.replace_after {
--- replace
        if now.saturating_sub(since) < self.replace_after * 1000 {
--- end
